WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:12.200
Batteries give off explosive hydrogen gas while charging, so battery compartments need ventilation, and batteries must be secured so they can’t shift in a seaway, with terminals covered.

2
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:19.300
Use marine-rated wiring, breakers and fuses, since many boat fires start with electrical faults.

3
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.625
Inspect shore power cords and connectors for heat damage.

4
00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:26.550
And remember electric shock drowning.

5
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:37.600
Faulty wiring can energize the water around docks, especially in fresh or brackish water, so never let anyone swim near a marina or dock with shore power.
